      "heading": "Which online therapy platform is best in 2026?",
      "body": "<p><strong>For most adults looking for talk therapy, betterhelp is the best starting point in 2026. It has the largest network in the category, matching that its own figures put at as little as two days, and live sessions by video, phone or chat with messaging between sessions. Talkspace is the better choice if you have insurance that covers it or if medication may be part of your care, because it is the only platform in our verified set that offers psychiatry on the same account. headspace belongs in a different category: it is a meditation and sleep app, and its therapy service is a separate product that accepts insurance.</strong></p>\n<p>That is the short answer, and it holds for most readers. The rest of this guide is for the people for whom it does not hold quite so neatly: someone who needs a prescriber, someone whose employer already pays for a platform, someone on a tight budget, someone who has used one app before and was disappointed. We have tried to make every claim checkable, to label company figures as company figures, and to say where we could not verify something.</p>"
