      "heading": "How did we choose and order the top three?",
      "body": "<p>We compared the platforms on the criteria a careful buyer would weigh, then ordered them by how well each fits the widest reasonable set of needs. The weights below are editorial judgment, stated openly so you can apply your own.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>What we checked</th><th>Source type</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Clinical credibility</td><td>Therapy must come from licensed clinicians</td><td>Licensing requirement, network size, platform scope</td><td>Platform information; state licensing boards</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Access and speed</td><td>A good plan you cannot start is no plan</td><td>Matching time, formats, scheduling</td><td>Company-stated figures, labeled</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Total cost</td><td>Price decides who can stay in therapy</td><td>Published self-pay plans, copays, financial aid</td><td>Verified where published; otherwise labeled</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Coverage often decides the real cost</td><td>Named plans, copay ranges, eligibility checks</td><td>Platform information; cited copays labeled</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Scope of care</td><td>Medication needs change the right answer</td><td>Psychiatry on-platform or not</td><td>Platform information</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Trust and privacy</td><td>Health data is sensitive</td><td>Regulatory history, Trustpilot profile</td><td>FTC release; Trustpilot captured Aug 2026</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two things we did not do. We did not rank by affiliate commission, and we did not rank by the number of positive reviews a platform could generate. A high rating from a curated sample is not the same as a high rating from the full review base, and we show both the platform-wide figure and the limits of our own sample in the review section below.</p>"
