      "heading": "#3 headspace: best for a daily mindfulness practice, not treatment",
      "body": "<p><strong>headspace is a meditation and sleep app first. It is the best-known product of its kind, and its own material cites more than 105 million app downloads. It also runs a separate online therapy service with licensed clinicians that accepts insurance. The two products have different prices, different billing and different purposes, and they should be judged separately. Its 1.5 Trustpilot score is the lowest of the three, and we report it as it is.</strong></p>\n\n<h3>Verified facts</h3>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Figure or fact</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>App downloads</td><td>More than 105 million</td><td>Company-cited</td></tr>\n<tr><td>App content</td><td>Guided meditation, sleep and stress content</td><td>Platform information</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Therapy service</td><td>Licensed clinicians by video; accepts insurance with a coverage check on its site</td><td>Platform information</td></tr>\n<tr><td>App billing</td><td>Consumer subscription; HSA/FSA eligible; not billed to insurance</td><td>Platform information; confirm with your administrator</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Psychiatry</td><td>Not offered by the therapy service</td><td>Platform information</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Trustpilot</td><td>1.5 across 770 reviews</td><td>Captured August 2026</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Strengths</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A practice you can start today.</strong> The guided content is designed for short, daily use, and its sleep and stress material suits people who want a routine rather than a clinician.</li>\n<li><strong>Therapy with insurance, separately.</strong> If you decide you need a clinician, the therapy service accepts insurance, so you do not have to buy the app to access it.</li>\n<li><strong>HSA and FSA eligibility.</strong> Depending on your administrator, the app may be payable from pre-tax accounts.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Trade-offs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>It is not treatment.</strong> An app is a practice tool. It cannot diagnose or treat a clinical condition, and it should sit alongside therapy rather than replace it.</li>\n<li><strong>The rating is low for a popular product.</strong> A 1.5 average across 770 reviews is strikingly low. Consumer subscription companies often receive low scores for billing and renewal complaints, so read recent reviews and the renewal terms before you subscribe.</li>\n<li><strong>Two products, one name.</strong> The app and the therapy service are priced and billed separately. Confusing them is the most common error buyers make.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Who should choose headspace</h3>\n<p>headspace suits people who want a daily mindfulness and sleep habit, people whose employer already includes it, and people who want to try structured practice before deciding whether they need therapy. It is the wrong choice if you need a clinician today and have not yet decided whether you need one, because the app will not give you that clinical care, and the therapy service is a separate purchase to compare against betterhelp and Talkspace.</p>"
