      "heading": "Final verdict and next steps",
      "body": "<p><strong>The best online therapy platform in 2026 depends on what you need, and that is an honest answer rather than a dodge. betterhelp is the best starting point for flexible talk therapy with the largest network. Talkspace is the better choice for insurance coverage and for anyone who may need medication. headspace is a daily practice app that happens to have a separate therapy service, and it should be judged on that basis.</strong></p>\n<p>Before you pay anyone, take these steps in order. Each one is quick, and together they replace most of the uncertainty in this guide with your own numbers.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Ask HR about your EAP.</strong> A set number of free sessions may already be part of your benefits.</li>\n<li><strong>Run the eligibility check on each platform</strong> you are considering, using your real member details. It replaces our typical figures with yours.</li>\n<li><strong>Read the cancellation, pause and privacy terms</strong> on the platform you choose. Billing complaints are the most common source of regret across this category.</li>\n<li><strong>Give the first therapist two sessions.</strong> If the fit is wrong, switch. On the major platforms that is free.</li>\n<li><strong>If medication may be part of your care</strong>, choose a platform with a prescriber, or plan a prescriber from the start.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep the crisis route close.</strong> Save 988 in your phone. In immediate danger, call 911.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Our <a href=\"/\">homepage ranking</a>, <a href=\"/reviews\">platform reviews</a> and <a href=\"/articles/online-therapy-guide\">complete guide to online therapy</a> go deeper on each step, and our <a href=\"/how-we-rank\">methodology page</a> explains how we weigh the criteria above.</p>\n<p>This guide is general information, not medical or financial advice. Prices, insurance terms and platform policies change, and the figures here were verified or captured on the dates shown. If you are in crisis in the US, call or text 988, or call 911 in immediate danger.</p>"
